          },
          {
            "source": "L1.5",
            "quote": "The side walls shall have vent slots that give at least 300 square millimetres of open area above the fan's mid-plane for intake and at least 300 square millimetres of open area below the fan for exhaust, with slots 2 to 3 mm wide and at least 1.5 mm of wall between slots, the intake and the exhaust vents each on at least two different walls, and no vent in the front panel, lid or floor."
          },
          {
            "source": "L1.5",
            "quote": "Intake means vents whose area-weighted centre is above the fan's mid-plane, exhaust means at or below the fan's exhaust face, and no vent may straddle the fan's frame between them."
          },
          {
            "source": "L1.6",
            "quote": "A continuous air path shall exist from the intake vents through the fan to the exhaust vents past the Pi, wide enough for a 5 mm sphere to roll through the inside of the case: from a vent's inner mouth to the centre of the 5 mm air gap above the fan inlet, and from the centre of the 5 mm air gap below the fan exhaust past the Pi to an exhaust vent's inner mouth (the slots themselves are sized by the vent rule)."
          },
          {
            "source": "L1.11",
            "quote": "The closed case shall have no openings other than the window, the encoder hole, the two USB openings and the vents, and its walls, floor and lid shall be 2 to 4 mm thick."
          }
